"routing_scope" = "Order: 21 cloud video exceptions → 194 AI / named Home entries (plus the Anthropic address range) → explicit cloud list → everything else direct. Matched traffic that fails is blocked, never retried directly; matched UDP/QUIC is refused so apps fall back to TCP. Apps using ECH, their own DNS-over-HTTPS, or cached addresses can hide an AI service; that traffic then goes direct. Unrecognised AI is not guaranteed to use Home.";
"routing_platform" = "On iPhone, all apps, all TCP/UDP ports, IPv4 and IPv6 enter the tunnel. LAN, link-local and multicast stay outside, as do Apple push and cellular services (calls, SMS). DNS for direct names uses your network's resolver; matched names never reach it. iOS has no per-app rules: Tono recognises AI only by domain and the Anthropic address range, and cannot exclude or include individual apps.";
